{%- comment -%}
  Renders the lab-grown marker that sits under a product thumbnail.

  A piece is lab-grown in more than one way in this catalog, and the marker
  misses stock when only one spelling is checked:
    - product type "Lab-Grown Diamond" (loose stones from the feed)
    - tags "Lab Grown Diamond", "Lab-Grown Diamond", or "lab-grown"
    - vendor "Peaceful Diamonds"
    - a title or handle that says lab-grown, for finished jewelry that
      carries the words in the name (solitaire rings, for example) and not
      the canonical tag

  Matching is case-insensitive, same as the product education block.
  A natural stone whose title, tags, type, and handle do not say lab-grown
  stays unmarked. The description is not read, so a comparison sentence
  on a natural piece cannot light the marker.

  Usage: {% render 'lab-grown-tag', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign lab_tags = product.tags | join: '||' | downcase
  assign lab_title = product.title | downcase
  assign lab_type = product.type | downcase
  assign lab_vendor = product.vendor | downcase
  assign lab_handle = product.handle | downcase
  assign lab_hay = lab_title | append: '||' | append: lab_tags | append: '||' | append: lab_type | append: '||' | append: lab_handle
  assign is_lab_grown = false
  if lab_vendor == 'peaceful diamonds'
    assign is_lab_grown = true
  elsif lab_hay contains 'lab grown' or lab_hay contains 'lab-grown' or lab_hay contains 'lab created' or lab_hay contains 'lab-created' or lab_handle contains 'lg-' or lab_handle contains 'lab-diamond'
    assign is_lab_grown = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_lab_grown -%}
  <span class="lab-grown-tag">Lab Grown Diamond</span>
{%- endif -%}
